# Titan Orbit UI — dark space gamer theme (MANDATORY)

When creating or restyling **any** player-facing UI (HUD, menus, tooltips, panels, loading, orbit station, upgrade trees), treat it as a **sci-fi game cockpit**, not a website, spreadsheet, or productivity app.

Paired chrome helpers: `ShipStatTooltipChrome`, `ShipAbilityCategoryColors`, `SpinCardShiftVisuals`. Prefer reusing those over inventing a second palette.

---

## Visual north star

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| Near-black void panels, deep navy glass | White / light gray / cream panels |
| Thin cyan / ice-blue accents on edges | Thick neon rainbow glow spam |
| Uppercase telemetry captions (`ABILITY MATRIX`) | Soft SaaS titles (`Settings`, `Details`) |
| Corner HUD + overlay cards | Centered “modal dialog” for gameplay chrome |
| Progress bars, ranks, XP, unlock states | Plain unlabeled number dumps |
| High-contrast body text on dark fill | Gray-on-gray or dark text on dark |

**Default panel fill** (match tooltip chrome): ~`RGB(0.012, 0.016, 0.028)` opaque.  
**Caption / rail text**: cool blue-gray (`~0.62, 0.78, 0.95`).  
**Body text**: near-white blue (`~0.88, 0.92, 0.98`).  
**Accent stripe**: thin top/side rail only — category color from `ShipAbilityCategoryColors` when the panel is about a ship stat.

---

## Gamification & gamer layout (required)

1. **Hierarchy like a HUD** — critical combat/status top or corners; secondary menus as slide-ins / overlays; never a flat form stack of equal-weight rows.
2. **Feedback loops** — show progress (bars, fills, `%`, unlock tiers), deltas (`+12 FP`), and state (LOCKED / READY / MAX) whenever the player can improve something.
3. **Readable combat info** — short labels (`FP`, `MS`) + full names on hover; color-code by category (offense/defense/energy/mobility/capacity).
4. **Game language** — “telemetry”, “matrix”, “loadout”, “orbit station”, “rank”, “boost” over “form”, “dialog”, “widget”, “admin”.
5. **Dense but scannable** — section banners / dividers inside one card (see `AppendSectionBanner` pattern); avoid sparse whitespace-heavy marketing layouts.
6. **Mobile + desktop** — keep the same dark theme; scale hit targets, don’t switch to a light “mobile web” skin.

---

## Forbidden UI looks

- Material / Fluent / Bootstrap-style light cards with drop shadows
- Purple-on-white gradients, warm cream paper themes, newspaper hairline layouts
- Bright opaque “Filled” Shift sprites as whole-panel backgrounds (washes out text — use dark glass fill)
- Emoji as primary decoration; candy pastel buttons; pill-chip spam
- Treating menus like CRUD tables (Excel grids) without game framing

---

## Agent checklist (before finishing UI work)

- [ ] Panel backgrounds are **dark space glass**, not light surfaces
- [ ] Accents are **thin rails / category tints**, not full-panel color floods
- [ ] Layout reads as **HUD / cockpit / loadout**, not settings form
- [ ] Upgradable or scored content shows **progress / rank / delta** where it fits
- [ ] Reused `ShipStatTooltipChrome` / `ShipAbilityCategoryColors` when building tooltips or stat chrome
- [ ] Captions use **uppercase game tone**; body stays high-contrast on dark
- [ ] Educational comments still apply (`titan-orbit-educational-comments.mdc`) — teach *what the player sees*

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — corporate light card
panel.color = new Color(0.95f, 0.95f, 0.97f, 0.95f);
title.text = "Details";

// ✅ GOOD — dark void glass + gamer caption
panel.color = new Color(0.012f, 0.016f, 0.028f, 1f);
caption.text = "TELEMETRY";
accent.color = ShipAbilityCategoryColors.GetPowerBreakdownStatColorForHud(statIndex);
```
